        a                              ecrm:E22_Man-Made_Object ;
        rdfs:comment                   "Dress fabric of brocaded silk, Spitalfields, 1745"@en , "Dress fabric of cream silk taffeta brocaded in coloured silks with a large central floral spray and two smaller ones. Linking the floral details is a self-coloured pattern of a cord with tassels and a pineapple flanked by ears of corn. The central spray is tied with a self-coloured ribbon and contains three heads of hops and there are more hops in the self-coloured pattern. \n\nIt is tabby brocaded with an additional flushing weft and has selvages with one green stripe and three outer cords."@en ;
        ecrm:P138i_has_representation  <http://data.silknow.org/image/5ec0286b-1308-352b-851c-1ca9b650bcc6> ;
        ecrm:P3_has_note               "Dress fabric of brocaded silk, Spitalfields, 1745"@en , "Dress fabric of cream silk taffeta brocaded in coloured silks with a large central floral spray and two smaller ones. Linking the floral details is a self-coloured pattern of a cord with tassels and a pineapple flanked by ears of corn. The central spray is tied with a self-coloured ribbon and contains three heads of hops and there are more hops in the self-coloured pattern. \n\nIt is tabby brocaded with an additional flushing weft and has selvages with one green stripe and three outer cords."@en ;
